(328438, 25166, 3080, '<td valign="top">Focus and clarity are better on the guy in back.  If you are the guy in front, I would hve either blurred out the background, or told your buddy to move.  Light coming through the right is quite a bit too bright, but  the shot is definately different.  Just think that the guy in back is taking away from the guy in front.  If you are the guy in the back, than the guy shouldn''t be in front.  One or the other.<br/>~Heather~</td>', 'Focus and clarity are better on the guy in back.  If you are the guy in front, I would hve either blurred out the background, or told your buddy to move.  Light coming through the right is quite a bit too bright, but  the shot is definately different.  Just think that the guy in back is taking away from the guy in front.  If you are the guy in the back, than the guy shouldn''t be in front.  One or the other.~Heather~', '2003-06-18 01:41:04.000000', NULL, 1),
