(336893, 25304, 6696, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Joy!</td>', 'Congratulations Joy!', '2003-06-25 01:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(336894, 24723, 9331, '<td valign="top">WOW - I''m so happy :)<br/>Thanks for all the great comments. This was my first challenge entry and to come 17th on my first go was a great achievement.<br/>I''m puzzled by the big difference in high and low scores<br/>Twelve 10''s and six 1''s - I would have loved to have got a comment for any of the 1''s or 2''s to find out why this didn''t meet the challenge.<br/>Any ideas, please post them here <br/> <br/>Richard</td>', 'WOW - I''m so happy :)Thanks for all the great comments. This was my first challenge entry and to come 17th on my first go was a great achievement.I''m puzzled by the big difference in high and low scoresTwelve 10''s and six 1''s - I would have loved to have got a comment for any of the 1''s or 2''s to find out why this didn''t meet the challenge.Any ideas, please post them here  Richard', '2003-06-25 01:17:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(336895, 24569, 2586, '<td valign="top">Hey Rob, you did quite well. Congrats. Really hope i didn''t offend you by calling the guy in the middle a scary sob :) That''s the result of the middle getting the longest exposure. I''m sure you look just dandy in real life. Am curious now though how you really look like. Hope you post a picture sometime somewhere :)</td>', 'Hey Rob, you did quite well. Congrats. Really hope i didn''t offend you by calling the guy in the middle a scary sob :) That''s the result of the middle getting the longest exposure. I''m sure you look just dandy in real life. Am curious now though how you really look like. Hope you post a picture sometime somewhere :)', '2003-06-25 01:17:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(336899, 24716, 2586, '<td valign="top">Hi Julia, what''s wrong? You got clothes on! :) I liked this portrait and the effect you accomplished. Thanks for posting the recipe. I''ll try it out myself sometime. I know you''re quite a modern woman but in this picture your looks are Pre-Raphaelite. Take care.</td>', 'Hi Julia, what''s wrong? You got clothes on! :) I liked this portrait and the effect you accomplished. Thanks for posting the recipe. I''ll try it out myself sometime. I know you''re quite a modern woman but in this picture your looks are Pre-Raphaelite. Take care.', '2003-06-25 01:21:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(336910, 24661, 1031, '<td valign="top">I really think your "vision" need not exclude DPC, it just may preclude more ribbons until the site (and the voters) progress further.</td>', 'I really think your "vision" need not exclude DPC, it just may preclude more ribbons until the site (and the voters) progress further.', '2003-06-25 01:23:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(336932, 25297, 7711, '<td valign="top">I guess no one DID get this picture. *sigh*<br/> <br/>Looking at this reminds me of what Setz wrote in his photographer notes for his self portrait... sometimes its just a damn interesting picture butr its not stock photography. This is a cool technique that you''ve managed to get a handle on and I like the message this image conveys. Good shot and be proud!</td>', 'I guess no one DID get this picture. *sigh* Looking at this reminds me of what Setz wrote in his photographer notes for his self portrait... sometimes its just a damn interesting picture butr its not stock photography. This is a cool technique that you''ve managed to get a handle on and I like the message this image conveys. Good shot and be proud!', '2003-06-25 01:28:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(336952, 24838, 3102, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the explanation -- I wondered how you pulled this off.  Great work -- congrats!</td>', 'Thanks for the explanation -- I wondered how you pulled this off.  Great work -- congrats!', '2003-06-25 01:32:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(336970, 25309, 2586, '<td valign="top">This pic is terribly, terribly underrated. I liked it a lot and gave it a high score for this challenge. Actually like how the hair is blowing all over a face and yet there is a lot of visibility of the facial features. Liked how the light (sunlight?) is playing through your hair and particularly how it shines through the background. Also liked the expression on your face. Found this portrait sexy in a quiet, understated way. Great job!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-06-25 00:38:44.</i></td>', 'This pic is terribly, terribly underrated. I liked it a lot and gave it a high score for this challenge. Actually like how the hair is blowing all over a face and yet there is a lot of visibility of the facial features. Liked how the light (sunlight?) is playing through your hair and particularly how it shines through the background. Also liked the expression on your face. Found this portrait sexy in a quiet, understated way. Great job!', '2003-06-25 01:37:19.000000', '2003-06-25 01:38:44.000000', 0),
(336972, 24661, 4494, '<td valign="top">Setzler, it''s you!  I''m sorry to hear you won''t be participating in challenges anymore, we are going to miss your great work.  I hope you change your mind and decide to participate from time to time.  Your work and participation really inspires a lot of people here so I''d hate to see you less active. :(<br/> <br/>I understand however.  I wish Drew and Langdon would consider ways for adding another demension to the DPChallenge by possibly adding a new type of challenge geared towards beginner "photo art" with no rules.  Then it could evolve from their to intermediate, etc.  I wouldn''t want that to be the focus of the site, but I think it could add a great new aspect to DPC.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Setzler, it''s you!  I''m sorry to hear you won''t be participating in challenges anymore, we are going to miss your great work.  I hope you change your mind and decide to participate from time to time.  Your work and participation really inspires a lot of people here so I''d hate to see you less active. :( I understand however.  I wish Drew and Langdon would consider ways for adding another demension to the DPChallenge by possibly adding a new type of challenge geared towards beginner "photo art" with no rules.  Then it could evolve from their to intermediate, etc.  I wouldn''t want that to be the focus of the site, but I think it could add a great new aspect to DPC.  ', '2003-06-25 01:37:42.000000', NULL, 0),
