(337730, 24644, 7966, '<td valign="top">I wish I could have reduced the glare in my glass (which was the #1 seggestion from those who commented) but from what I understand it''s against the rules to edit stuff like that.<br/>I think the photo came out suprisingly well for the little effort I put into it. It was taken around 7 am on a Sunday, I had no make up on and didn''t even really brush my hair. The lighting was all natural, just the sun coming through the bay window in my living room. I was sitting on the couch. <br/>Thank you for all your comments!</td>', 'I wish I could have reduced the glare in my glass (which was the #1 seggestion from those who commented) but from what I understand it''s against the rules to edit stuff like that.I think the photo came out suprisingly well for the little effort I put into it. It was taken around 7 am on a Sunday, I had no make up on and didn''t even really brush my hair. The lighting was all natural, just the sun coming through the bay window in my living room. I was sitting on the couch. Thank you for all your comments!', '2003-06-25 12:24:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(337732, 25290, 8610, '<td valign="top">You win some and you loose some. It was a pratice shot for my to take picture whith shutter speed longer than 1/30. I got some better technic now and learn alot since I took this picture few days ago. Might be a litle sharper though...<br/> <br/>Thanx for the comment ppl. And the peoble who had fun of this picture</td>', 'You win some and you loose some. It was a pratice shot for my to take picture whith shutter speed longer than 1/30. I got some better technic now and learn alot since I took this picture few days ago. Might be a litle sharper though... Thanx for the comment ppl. And the peoble who had fun of this picture', '2003-06-25 12:25:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(337799, 24838, 8860, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jonpink:</b></div><hr/><i>good idea, the face spoils it though (only in my opinion) as it''s very noisy an a bit wishy washy.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with this - and for me the face should have matched the rest of the image quality (it being a self-portrait challenge and all!). The bulb itself is great.</td>', 'Originally posted by jonpink:good idea, the face spoils it though (only in my opinion) as it''s very noisy an a bit wishy washy.  I agree with this - and for me the face should have matched the rest of the image quality (it being a self-portrait challenge and all!). The bulb itself is great.', '2003-06-25 13:17:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(337812, 25179, 6900, '<td valign="top">I wonder if K-Rob and all the doubters are enjoying the taste of the foot in his mouth right now.<br/>Cable to trigger the timer, drop the cable?  Easily possible people, c''mon.<br/> <br/>Great shot - and I''m glad to see it was you who took it.  A lot of people know you and your brother from previous pictures, but people get really weird sometimes when they think they know something they don''t really know.<br/> <br/>Good work!<br/></td>', 'I wonder if K-Rob and all the doubters are enjoying the taste of the foot in his mouth right now.Cable to trigger the timer, drop the cable?  Easily possible people, c''mon. Great shot - and I''m glad to see it was you who took it.  A lot of people know you and your brother from previous pictures, but people get really weird sometimes when they think they know something they don''t really know. Good work!', '2003-06-25 13:27:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(337823, 25263, 2152, '<td valign="top">Thanks Jacko - and everyone else who left a comment.  I figured all most people would see would be a dark, grainy, out of focus shot - that''s to be expected here.  But some people "got it" and that''s all I was hoping for.<br/> <br/>Ozdick, i can assure you I was drinking and if the bottle was at any more of an angle, it might have been a shot of me puking in bed.<br/> <br/>So... anyone want a print of this?</td>', 'Thanks Jacko - and everyone else who left a comment.  I figured all most people would see would be a dark, grainy, out of focus shot - that''s to be expected here.  But some people "got it" and that''s all I was hoping for. Ozdick, i can assure you I was drinking and if the bottle was at any more of an angle, it might have been a shot of me puking in bed. So... anyone want a print of this?', '2003-06-25 13:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(337824, 25297, 6900, '<td valign="top">Lots of people asked for directions on how to do my self portrait:<br/> <br/>I set up my cam on a tripod within arms reach.  Then I put a red light bulb in my desk lamp.  I put the lamp almost in my lap and the cam right behind it.<br/> <br/>Set the cam to manual: 4 seconds, f7.1 aperture, 100 ISO, then I <br/> <br/>1. Set the timer.  Popped up the flash.<br/>2. Half pushed the button to focus with the red light on.<br/>3. Turned the red light off. <br/>4. Pushed the button.<br/>5. As soon as it flashed, I turned the red light on with my left hand and moved slightly to the left with my eyes closed, then opened them. (for the last 3.8 seconds or so)<br/> <br/>That''s pretty much it.  The original with exif is <a href="//www.pbase.com/image/18252879&amp;exif=Y\" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.pbase.com/image/18252879&amp;exif=Y\</a></td>', 'Lots of people asked for directions on how to do my self portrait: I set up my cam on a tripod within arms reach.  Then I put a red light bulb in my desk lamp.  I put the lamp almost in my lap and the cam right behind it. Set the cam to manual: 4 seconds, f7.1 aperture, 100 ISO, then I  1. Set the timer.  Popped up the flash.2. Half pushed the button to focus with the red light on.3. Turned the red light off. 4. Pushed the button.5. As soon as it flashed, I turned the red light on with my left hand and moved slightly to the left with my eyes closed, then opened them. (for the last 3.8 seconds or so) That''s pretty much it.  The original with exif is //www.pbase.com/image/18252879&exif=Y\', '2003-06-25 13:35:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(337860, 24838, 8713, '<td valign="top">How did you suspend the lightbulb in the air?</td>', 'How did you suspend the lightbulb in the air?', '2003-06-25 13:58:42.000000', NULL, 0),
