(555354, 25189, 15703, '<td valign="top">I think the use of grain here is the very thing that makes it NOT a re-hash of the old self-photo. The excellent moody lighting adds yet more mood to that created by the sinister spectacles. The fingers on the camera have a nicely dynamic, but natural, position. For me, this picture comes together very nicely indeed.</td>', 'I think the use of grain here is the very thing that makes it NOT a re-hash of the old self-photo. The excellent moody lighting adds yet more mood to that created by the sinister spectacles. The fingers on the camera have a nicely dynamic, but natural, position. For me, this picture comes together very nicely indeed.', '2004-01-24 12:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(555426, 25272, 15703, '<td valign="top">The brown frame really complements your hair and skin. The scene is a micro-dab too bright, but your framing and expression really make this a great shot. I totally love it. I am intrigued at your confident choice of clothing. I wonder if you are illustrating the "bad hair" message while working tirelessly on it in the bathroom?</td>', 'The brown frame really complements your hair and skin. The scene is a micro-dab too bright, but your framing and expression really make this a great shot. I totally love it. I am intrigued at your confident choice of clothing. I wonder if you are illustrating the "bad hair" message while working tirelessly on it in the bathroom?', '2004-01-24 14:12:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(555433, 25235, 15703, '<td valign="top">Classically, far too dark. But, for me, it gains a really moody and arty feel. I think you were very brave to take the light so low, but I think it''s a great shot. The image is a little bit soft, but nothing a little sharpening wouldn''t put right. Fortunately, with such a dark image, there isn''t too much that needs to be sharpened! A fabulous submission.</td>', 'Classically, far too dark. But, for me, it gains a really moody and arty feel. I think you were very brave to take the light so low, but I think it''s a great shot. The image is a little bit soft, but nothing a little sharpening wouldn''t put right. Fortunately, with such a dark image, there isn''t too much that needs to be sharpened! A fabulous submission.', '2004-01-24 14:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(555437, 24769, 15703, '<td valign="top">Like Pedro has said, I think the title of this shot lifts it up into a very personal image. The image itself is a little edgy and reportage-y, which is no bad thing!  Excellent.</td>', 'Like Pedro has said, I think the title of this shot lifts it up into a very personal image. The image itself is a little edgy and reportage-y, which is no bad thing!  Excellent.', '2004-01-24 14:39:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(555687, 25235, 16188, '<td valign="top">To me, it doesn''t matter if a picture breaks rules as long as it works visually.  And by that I mean, that it works on an aesthetic level for me, since I can''t speak for anyone else.  I love this picture.</td>', 'To me, it doesn''t matter if a picture breaks rules as long as it works visually.  And by that I mean, that it works on an aesthetic level for me, since I can''t speak for anyone else.  I love this picture.', '2004-01-24 22:43:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(589718, 25113, 16188, '<td valign="top">I love this self-portrait and those pictures look pretty interesting!  Thanks for your comment on my agave image in the Textures challenge, by the way... most people are saying things like ''that''s the wrong color, you ought to change it in PS'' and ''where''s the texture?'' so I really loved your reaction. :)  I guess it takes someone who knows what agave are like to appreciate that picture. Thanks so much for posting. :)  (P.S. My husband is a photographer too and he works primarily in medium and large format, the latter on an old wood and brass Wista.  He liked seeing your camera with the red bellows! :)</td>', 'I love this self-portrait and those pictures look pretty interesting!  Thanks for your comment on my agave image in the Textures challenge, by the way... most people are saying things like ''that''s the wrong color, you ought to change it in PS'' and ''where''s the texture?'' so I really loved your reaction. :)  I guess it takes someone who knows what agave are like to appreciate that picture. Thanks so much for posting. :)  (P.S. My husband is a photographer too and he works primarily in medium and large format, the latter on an old wood and brass Wista.  He liked seeing your camera with the red bellows! :)', '2004-02-20 02:04:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(612735, 25037, 669, '<td valign="top">Interesting use of grain..  Not sure if this was intentional or not, but it definitely adds something to the shot, particularly with the choice of sepia.  I like the soft focus, it suits the shot well. Like some of your other shots there''s good contrast and brightness.  I''m not sure about the composition.  I think a longer necklace may have added interest.  All in all, good shot, and extra kudos for bravery!</td>', 'Interesting use of grain..  Not sure if this was intentional or not, but it definitely adds something to the shot, particularly with the choice of sepia.  I like the soft focus, it suits the shot well. Like some of your other shots there''s good contrast and brightness.  I''m not sure about the composition.  I think a longer necklace may have added interest.  All in all, good shot, and extra kudos for bravery!', '2004-03-07 11:25:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(617311, 24661, 17525, '<td valign="top">thanks John, these are lovely and inspiring words!</td>', 'thanks John, these are lovely and inspiring words!', '2004-03-10 18:12:27.000000', NULL, 0),
